Implement user story AMSD-1820: [Mozio] - The Promo code amount is NOT displayed as expected for Return trip tickets in the Mozio email confirmation

## Story Description
The promo code discount amount is not displayed correctly for return trip tickets in the Mozio email confirmation. The root cause is in how the per-unit discount is calculated for return trip segments and how the discount field is propagated from the dispatch report into the sanitized Mozio dispatch. The fix must ensure the discount is correctly calculated and propagated for both outbound and return segments of a return trip.

## Acceptance Criteria
- Given a return trip ticket order with a promo code applied, when the Mozio email confirmation is generated, then the promo code discount amount appears for both the outbound and return trip segments.
- Given a return trip ticket order with a promo code applied, when the Mozio email confirmation is generated, then the sum of the discount amounts shown for the outbound and return segments equals the total promo code discount applied to the order.
- Given a return trip ticket order with a promo code applied only to the return leg, when the Mozio email confirmation is generated, then the return trip segment shows a discount amount and the outbound segment shows no discount.
- Given a return trip ticket order with a promo code applied only to the outbound leg, when the Mozio email confirmation is generated, then the outbound trip segment shows a discount amount and the return segment shows no discount.
- Given a return trip ticket order with no promo code applied, when the Mozio email confirmation is generated, then neither the outbound nor the return trip segment shows a discount amount.
- Given a one-way trip ticket order with a promo code applied, when the Mozio email confirmation is generated, then the discount amount matches the promo code value applied to the order (regression check).
- Given a return trip ticket order with a promo code applied, when the Mozio email confirmation is generated, then the discount amount displayed for each segment is never a negative value.
- Given a return trip ticket order with a promo code applied, when the Mozio email confirmation is generated, then the discount amount for each segment is formatted consistently with other monetary values in the same email confirmation.


## Root Cause Analysis (ALREADY INVESTIGATED — start here, do not re-trace)
A code investigation already traced this bug to its cause. Apply the fix at the location(s) below; do NOT re-read the whole codebase to re-derive this — the analysis is done:
- **src/services/order-staff-notes/generate-staff-notes.mappers.ts** (`getTicketPricePerUnit`): Computes the discount per unit for return trip segments (isReturnTrip=true) by halving base and selling then deriving discount = base - selling. This is where the wrong discount value originates — the calculation logic for how the promo discount is split across outbound/return segments.
- **src/services/submit-reservations/apply-report-discounts.service.ts** (`applyReportDiscountsService`): Writes dispatch.report.price.discount on the Mozio dispatch payload. This is where the discount is ASSIGNED to the dispatch object that mapToSanitizedMozioDispatch later reads from. If the discount is missing or wrong for return-trip dispatches, the cause is here — it determines which dispatches get a discount applied and how much.
- **src/clients/mozio/mappers/map-to-sanitized-mozio-dispatch.ts** (`mapToSanitizedMozioDispatch`): Propagates dispatch.report.price.discount to the sanitized Mozio dispatch used in the email confirmation. It only reads and passes through the discount — if the upstream dispatch lacks the correct discount for return-trip segments, this mapper will propagate the wrong/missing value. The fix here ensures the discount field is correctly mapped for both outbound and return segments.

